<title>UK: UK's Lang &quot;very surprised&quot; by EC view on BA/AA.</title>
<headline>UK's Lang &quot;very surprised&quot; by EC view on BA/AA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>President of the UK board of trade, Ian Lang, said on his return trip from a tour of India, Pakistan and Bangladesh with prime minister John Major that he was &quot;very surprised&quot; by the European Commission's opposition to clearing the British Airways and American Airlines ZAMR.L deal on terms laid out by the UK government.</p>
<p>He said he would not comment further until he had seen the letter sent to him by EC competition commissioner Karel van Miert who said the EC would defend its view in the European Court of Justice if necessary.</p>
<p>Lang added that the British parliament had taken powers with the agreement of the Commission to review the competitive aspects of the deal.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
